# What this engine says, case by case, for enus.
#
# Every line was blessed by IBM's own binary when it was
# first written: the whole differential suite was run
# for this language immediately before, and every case
# matched. A case a deliberate divergence has moved or
# added since is this engine's answer and not IBM's;
# docs/quirks.md names them. See docs/testing.md.
#
# The wide cases are the wideband voice, which IBM never
# made: an ear blessed them, not an original.
#
# Written by test/matrix.sh record. One line a case:
# the category, which case in it, the first sixteen hex of
# the samples' hash, the same of the reported answers', and
# the sentence.

plain 1 3ae4e03b58575154 28775d11629885cc Hello. This is the Eloquence synthesizer speaking.
plain 2 0455f430e860f421 903ce95c2021fc22 Dr. Smith paid $1,234.56 on 3rd May 2026 at 7:45 p.m.
plain 3 2385dbb5d8947b80 8b47a3bf7642bc2f The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog; e.g. www.example.com/path?q=1
plain 4 e7a11c93534f30c4 a1e5621c0f3ea2ab Testing 1 2 3, ABC XYZ, hyphenated-words and UPPERCASE.
plain 5 d4fe33fae44e4dd2 0510369e14ad1de4 A one-word line. And another; plus "quoted text" inside.
plain 6 850e6621c9099816 b1f160eedbd6aba1 Rzeczpospolita, naiveté, 42% of 3.14159, and Mr O'Brien-Smith Jr.
plain 7 29f67773bfed73f0 f65ca06ac278aa5c He said: don't! Then (parenthetically) 1/2 + 3/4 = 5/4; see p. 12.
plain 8 5e4e4261780111e4 b95269c27c9fd588 A 5,000-strong crowd raised 1,000,500 dollars, and the fund reached 25,000,000.
plain 9 6f17588546ca3622 5e181ee1a2c85cca Windows10 and teamtalk5 are words with a version, and MP3, utf8 and H2O are spelled.
plain 10 c46b89f0b7078a27 ca4da7d34c29ca65 Call this(thing) or sum(x) for each friend(s), item#3 at price$5, and AUD$5 too.
